{
  "_comment": "What may be scanned (#614, #748). One decision, in open-security-shared/target_policy.py, used by the tools service (open-security-tools/app/target_policy.py) and by guardian (open-security-guardian/apps/assets/networks.py). Three suites run these cases, each through its own entry point, so the three agree: tests/shared/test_target_policy.py, open-security-tools/tests/unit/test_target_policy_vectors.py and open-security-guardian/tests/unit/test_scan_target_policy.py. 'allow' is the operator's allowlist for the case (empty when absent): CIDR ranges and IP addresses only, since guardian takes no host name. 'expect' is 'allowed', 'internal', 'too_large' or 'invalid'. For a refused range, 'address' is the first address of it the policy refuses. No case here depends on the Python version: an IPv6 address that embeds a public IPv4 one is left out, because versions disagree on whether its prefix is global.",
